<section class="module-landing-banner mb-5" style="--hero-bg: url('../images/modules/sector-construction.png');" aria-label="Introduction">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="module-landing-accent" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p class="module-landing-kicker mb-2">Construction & Engineering</p>
        <h1 class="module-landing-headline text-white mb-3">Construction Management Software for Project Control.</h1>
        <p class="module-landing-dek mb-4 col-lg-10 px-0">
            Managing complex construction projects requires a unified platform that connects the office to the field, 
            ensuring that budgets, schedules, and quality standards are maintained from groundbreaking to handover.
        </p>
        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <a href="#components" class="btn btn-light btn-sm px-4 fw-semibold">Module components</a>
            <a href="/#inquiry" class="btn btn-outline-light btn-sm px-4">Start a conversation</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="row mb-5" id="components">

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Module Components</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
            The construction management system comprises integrated components that streamline specialized workflows 
            across the project lifecycle. Each component addresses specific operational needs while contributing 
            to unified project reporting and control.
        </p>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-2"><a href="/construction/dashboard">Dashboard</a></h3>
                <p class="small">
                    Unified visibility into project performance through real-time dashboards aggregating data from 
                    field, office, and finance. Key health indicators signal performance variance, providing 
                    immediate awareness of cost and schedule status without manual report compilation.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-2"><a href="/construction/tendering">Tendering & Bidding</a></h3>
                <p class="small">
                    Structured opportunity tracking and digitised estimating workflows ensuring bid accuracy and 
                    profitability integrity. Material takeoff from Bills of Quantities (BOQ) applies current market 
                    rates for plant and labor reducing the risk of calculation errors in tender submissions.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-2"><a href="/construction/contracts">Contract Management</a></h3>
                <p class="small">
                    Lifecycle administration of client and vendor contracts within FIDIC or NEC frameworks. 
                    Variation order (VO) tracking ensures additional works are properly valued and approved, 
                    maintaining an immutable log of contractual correspondence and claims history.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-2"><a href="/construction/projectplanning">Project Planning</a></h3>
                <p class="small">
                    Integrated scheduling with Gantt charts and critical path method (CPM) analysis connecting baselines 
                    to site execution. Resource loading identifies potential bottlenecks while rolling look-ahead 
                    programmes provide granular detail for site coordination and milestone tracking.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-2"><a href="/construction/sitemanagement">Site Management</a></h3>
                <p class="small">
                    Real-time field data capture replacing paper logs with digital site diaries, resource logs, and 
                    inspection checklists. Time-stamped and geotagged entries provide an authentic record of site 
                    activity, progress, and safety incidents for comprehensive project documentation.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-2"><a href="/construction/subcontractors">Subcontractors</a></h3>
                <p class="small">
                    Comprehensive supply chain control through structured vetting, award management, and measured work 
                    valuations. Automated payment certificate calculation accounts for retentions and variations, 
                    identifying overclaims and ensuring transparent financial administration of vendors.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-2"><a href="/construction/costcontrol">Cost Control</a></h3>
                <p class="small">
                    Detailed job costing mapping expenditures to granular cost codes with committed cost tracking. 
                    Budget vs. actual variance analysis identifies early warning signs for overruns, while 
                    scientific cost-to-complete (CTC) forecasting clarifies project financial end-positions.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-2"><a href="/construction/progressbilling">Progress Billing</a></h3>
                <p class="small">
                    Monthly valuation processing accelerating cash flow through accurate claims for work completed 
                    and materials on site. Automated Interim Payment Certificate (IPC) generation eliminates 
                    arithmetic errors while retention schedules track release dates and obligations.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-2"><a href="/construction/safetyhealth">Safety & Health</a></h3>
                <p class="small">
                    Integrated safety management ensuring compliance with NSSA and OSHA standards through HIRA logs, 
                    incident reporting, and safety inductions. Integrated PPE registers and risk assessments 
                    embed health and safety protocols directly into the project's daily operational workflow.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Tendering and Estimating Integrity</h2>
        <p>
            The foundation of project profitability is established at the bid stage. Our system provides 
            a structured environment for capturing tender opportunities from IDBZ, local authorities, 
            and private clients. Digitised Bills of Quantities (BOQ) enable precise material takeoffs 
            and labor rate application, reducing the risk of errors that lead to loss-making contracts.
        </p>
        <p>
            Submit with confidence using accurate cost data and historical performance metrics. The 
            bid/no-bid workflow ensures that resources are focused on opportunities with the highest 
            probability of success and alignment with organizational capabilities.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Integrated Site and Field Operations</h2>
        <p>
            Capture the reality of the construction site as it happens. The digital site diary replaces 
            paper logs, tracking weather, resources on site, and work completed in real time. 
            Request for Information (RFI) registers and site instruction logs eliminate the 
            miscommunications that lead to delays and rework.
        </p>
        <p>
            Inspection checklists and photo logs ensure that quality standards are maintained and 
            documented throughout the project. This rigorous documentation provides the audit trail 
            necessary for variations, claims, and final account resolution.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Precision Cost Control and Job Costing</h2>
        <p>
            Move beyond simple accounting to detailed job costing. Our system tracks committed costs 
            from purchase orders and subcontractor awards, providing a true view of project 
            financial exposure before invoices even arrive. Cost variance analysis (budget vs. 
            committed vs. actual) identifies issues early, enabling corrective action.
        </p>
        <p>
            Earned Value Management (EVM) metrics including cost and schedule performance indices 
            provide a scientific view of project health. Cost-to-complete (CTC) forecasts 
            integrate field progress with remaining budget, ensuring that final project margins 
            are predictable and managed.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Contract Administration and Compliance</h2>
        <p>
            Manage contracts within the framework of FIDIC, NEC, or custom conditions. Variation order 
            management ensures that additional works are properly valued, approved, and incorporated 
            into the project budget. Contractual correspondence logs maintain a comprehensive 
            history of all project communication, providing essential support in the event of 
            disputes or claims.
        </p>
        <p>
            Monthly progress valuations and interim payment certificates align payments with measured 
            work on site. Retention tracking and release workflows ensure that contractual 
            obligations are met while protecting organization cash flow.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Safety, Health, and Environment (SHE)</h2>
        <p>
            Maintain compliance with NSSA, OSHA, and ISO 45001 standards through integrated safety 
            management. Record site inductions, PPE issuance, and hazard identification (HIRA) 
            directly in the system. Incident reporting and accident investigation workflows 
            ensure that safety events are documented and analyzed for future prevention.
        </p>
        <p>
            A strong safety record is not only a moral obligation but a significant competitive 
            advantage in modern construction tendering. Our system provides the data necessary 
            to demonstrate safety commitment to clients and regulators alike.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

